- op: discuss  # 1736
  at: '2026-06-02T03:52:46Z'  # 1736
  by: agent  # 1736
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1736
  clock: 3  # 1736
  nonce: '1736'  # 1736
  message: "Pass-22 investigation correction.\n\nThe original framing claimed the semantic difference between edge.id and edge.edge_key is 'not documented'. After reading ir.py:\n- Line 15 (module docstring): 'edges carry a structured ID and edge_key for deduplication across passes' — mentions both fields.\n- Line 583 (Edge dataclass docstring on edge_key): 'Canonical identity for deduplication across passes'.\n- Line 516 (_compute_edge_key): docstring 'Compute canonical edge_key for deduplication across passes'.\n- Line 693-697: edge_key is computed from (src + dst + edge_type), line-insensitive — so edge_key is the structural identity (excludes line for cross-pass dedup), while edge.id is the line-included instance identity.\n\nBoth ARE documented. The earlier 'documentation gap' framing was wrong.\n\nThe real (much weaker) residual: NAMING-CONVENTION divergence from Symbol's id/stable_id pair. Symbol has id (location-based) and stable_id (structural-identity hash). Edge has id (presumably instance-unique with line) and edge_key (structural identity for dedup). The structural-identity field is called stable_id on Symbol and edge_key on Edge — same semantic, different name.\n\nDowngrade P3 -> P4 cosmetic. Either rename edge.edge_key -> edge.stable_id to mirror Symbol's convention, or document explicitly in the IR docstring that edge_key is the Edge counterpart of Symbol.stable_id. Minor naming-axis-uniformity issue; not worth surfacing in agent notes table."  # 1736
