- op: discuss  # 6e83
  at: '2026-07-15T22:30:57Z'  # 6e83
  by: agent  # 6e83
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6e83
  clock: 5  # 6e83
  nonce: '6e83'  # 6e83
  message: "DOCUMENT verdict, shipped in the docs PR merged to dev as 37e0252d5b (commit bc366977). This item was already self-corrected on 2026-06-02 — both edge.id and edge_key ARE documented (ir.py Edge docstring). Verified live on hg-self-v5: edge.id = edge:sha256:<16hex> (134,805/134,805 populated, all distinct), edge_key = edgekey:sha256:<16hex> (134,805/134,805, all distinct). The sole residual was the missing naming-convention cross-reference. Resolution: added to the ir.py Edge docstring that edge_key is the structural-identity / cross-pass-dedup counterpart of Symbol.stable_id (line-insensitive, survives regeneration), while edge.id is the per-instance counterpart of Symbol.id. Renaming edge_key->stable_id for naming uniformity would be a breaking schema change touching every consumer — rejected; documented the equivalence instead."  # 6e83
